    Adapted for EJBCA CE 9.6.3 by the ejbca-custom project (https://github.com/3keyroman/ejbca-custom,
    commit 401887f, 2026-09-17), which changed the org.apache.commons.lang imports to lang3 and, in
    AzureCryptoToken, the KeyAndCertFinder.find result from Pair to KeyAndCertificateInfo. Copied here
    on 2026-09-18 with no further change; the comparison with the upstream commits above was redone
    then and shows exactly those differences and nothing else.

    One behavioural difference from what Community Edition 9.3.7 shipped. That release's compiled
    PKCS11CryptoToken overrode getKeyUsagesFromKey/PrivateKey/PublicKey to return an empty set. The
    2023 source does not, so on 9.6.3 the token inherits CryptoToken's new defaults, which infer the
    usage set from the key type. That is upstream's current behaviour for a token that cannot read
    CKA_* usage attributes, and it is what the Admin UI will show. See
    docs/EJBCA_UPSTREAM_WATCH.md.

StartupCheckPatcher.java, LinkCheck.java, build.sh

    Apache-2.0, Copyright (c) 2026 Thomas Pham, like the rest of kimbo11ng. StartupCheckPatcher
    rewrites one method of Keyfactor's ejbca-ejb.jar at image-build time; it contains none of
    Keyfactor's code. It uses ASM (BSD-3-Clause, https://asm.ow2.io), which build.sh downloads,
    checks against a pinned SHA-256 and uses without adding it to the image.

Do not redistribute the built image
-----------------------------------

The image this produces contains Keyfactor's ejbca-ejb.jar with a method removed, and the LGPL classes
above. The base image also carries jars that Keyfactor declares LGPL-2.1 and whose source is not
published (x509-common-util, cryptotokens-api, cryptotokens-impl, keyfactor-commons-cli). LGPL 2.1
section 4 makes whoever distributes a binary responsible for the matching source, which a downstream
party cannot supply. Build the image yourself, from source, for your own use.

